 "drivingQuestion": "What does the fire example add?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "The fire case teaches permission even for another courtyard.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "yoma.84b.11",
   "daf": "84b",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "מְכַבִּין וּמַפְסִיקִין. לְמָה לִי? דַּאֲפִילּוּ לְחָצֵר אַחֶרֶת.",
   "en": "It was taught in a baraita that «one» may «extinguish a fire» by «placing a barrier» in front of it on Shabbat. The Gemara asks: «Why do I» need «this?» What new point is taught by this additional case of a life-endangering situation? The Gemara answers: This halakha applies «even» if the fire is spreading «toward another courtyard.» Not only may this be done to save the lives of people in the courtyard on fire; it may also be done to prevent the fire from spreading to an adjacent courtyard."
  }
 ],
